186
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:29,820
We become part of our immediate environment.

187
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:35,400
None of us are immune to the influences of our own world, and let us not kid

188
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:39,640
ourselves that we are untouched by the things and the people in our life.

189
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:43,260
Fred goes off to his new job at a

190
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:49,000
Fred takes a 10 -minute coffee break, but the other workers take a half an hour.

191
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:52,460
Fred says, What's the matter with you guys?

192
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:56,080
Weeks later, Fred is taking 20 -minute breaks.

193
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:59,500
A month later, Fred takes his half hour.

194
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:03,480
Fred is saying, If you can't beat them, join them.

195
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,440
Why should I work any harder than the next guy?

196
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:12,180
The fascinating thing about being human is that generally we are unaware that there

197
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:14,300
are changes taking place in our mentality.

198
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:19,330
It is like returning to the city smog after some weeks in the fresh air.

199
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:24,800
Only then do we realize that we have become accustomed to the nasty smells.

200
00:19:25,940 --> 00:19:28,570
Mix with critical people, and we learn to criticize.

201
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:32,580
Mix with happy people, and we learn about happiness.

202
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:38,080
What this means is that we need to decide what we want from life, and then choose

203
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,440
our company accordingly.

204
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:43,480
You may well say, That is going to take some effort.

205
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:45,100
It may not be comfortable.

206
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:47,780
I may offend some of my present company.

207
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:50,600
Right, but it is your life.

208
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:56,720
Fred may say, I'm always broke, frequently depressed, I'm going nowhere, and I never

209
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,000
do anything exciting.

210
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:03,720
Then we discover that Fred's best friends are always broke, frequently depressed,

211
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,060
nowhere, and wishing that life was more exciting.

212
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:09,520
This is not coincidence.

213
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:13,680
Nor is it our business to stand in judgment of Fred.

214
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:18,680
However, if Fred ever wants to improve his quality of life, the first thing he'll

215
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:22,680
need to do is recognize what has been going on all these years.

216
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:28,460
It's no surprise that doctors, as a profession, suffer a lot of ill health, because

217
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:30,580
they spend their lives around sick people.

218
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:35,800
Psychiatrists have a higher incidence of suicide in their profession, for related

219
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:41,720
reasons. Traditionally, 9 out of 10 children whose parents smoke, smoke themselves.

220
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:45,780
Obesity is in part an environmental problem.

221
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:51,500
Successful people have successful friends, and so the story goes on.

